        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "1. A grievance arising out of the terms of this Agreement, which has been properly processed through the Grievance Procedure within the time limits specified and not settled, may be submitted to arbitration by approval of the Union's Executive Board or by the Management of the Employer. If an arbitrator is not selected at the conclusion of the Informal Arbitration Step of the Grievance Procedure, the Union shall have ten (10) working days to serve written notice to the Company of their intent to arbitrate.",
